[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/954045657","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1340#issuecomment-954045657","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1340","id":954045657,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE8443ZTZ","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-10-28T17:18:59Z","updated_at":"2021-10-28T17:18:59Z","body":"@samth - I'm unclear as where the actual license is??\r\n\r\n- https://schemers.org/Documents/Standards/R5RS/HTML/r5rs-Z-H-3.html#%_sec_Temp_4 - goes to a page with an intro, background, and acknowledgments (no license)\r\n- of the 3 examples you provide, one is Apache-2.0 OR MIT\r\n- the other two look to be papers that do not include license language\r\n??\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/954045657/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/954123743","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1340#issuecomment-954123743","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1340","id":954123743,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE8443sXf","user":{"login":"samth","id":244723,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NDcyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244723?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth","html_url":"https://github.com/samth","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-10-28T19:08:52Z","updated_at":"2021-10-28T19:08:52Z","body":"- The third paragraph of \"Background\" is the license text I quoted.\r\n- The example that you say is Apache or MIT has the following LICENSE file: https://github.com/racket/r6rs/blob/master/LICENSE which explicitly references the license under discussion.\r\n- The third example contains identical license language (see page 3 of https://small.r7rs.org/attachment/r7rs.pdf)\r\n- The license also appears identically on page 3 of the other document.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/954123743/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/965949928","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1340#issuecomment-965949928","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1340","id":965949928,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE845kzno","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-11-11T03:10:37Z","updated_at":"2021-11-11T03:10:37Z","body":"thanks @samth - sorry for missing that.\r\ncopying text here: \r\n\"We intend this report to belong to the entire Scheme community, and so we grant permission to copy it in whole or in part without fee. In particular, we encourage implementors of Scheme to use this report as a starting point for manuals and other documentation, modifying it as necessary.\"\r\n\r\nhere is a analysis based on our license inclusion principles (next comment)\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/965949928/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/965954420","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1340#issuecomment-965954420","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1340","id":965954420,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE845k0t0","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-11-11T03:22:08Z","updated_at":"2021-11-11T03:22:08Z","body":"* Has the license been approved by the OSI?\r\n  * no\r\n* Is the submitted license unique, that is, it does not match another license already on the License List as per the matching guidelines?\r\n  * it does not match anything currently on the SPDX License List\r\n* If a software license, does it apply to source code and not only to executables?\r\n  * it refers to a report (not software) \r\n* Does the license have identifiable and stable text, and is not in the midst of drafting?\r\n  * seems stable, yes\r\n* Has the license steward, if any, committed to versioning new versions in the future and to not modify it after addition to the list?\r\n  * not sure this is relevant, as it seems this is a one-off \r\n\r\nOther factors for inclusion\r\n1. Does the license substantially comply with one of the free/open content definitions?\r\nyes\r\n2. Does the license have substantial use such that it is likely to be encountered (ie. use in many projects, or in one significant project)?\r\nit has been in use for a long time, not sure how widespread it use is beyond the example cited here or how it being on the SPDX License List would help in identification given the text is usually incorporated in a paper? \r\n\r\n3. Is the license structured to be generally usable by anyone, and not specific to one organisation or project?\r\nit seem specific to these reports, probably not used otherwise\r\n\r\n4. Is the license primarily intended to facilitate the free distribution of content with limited restrictions?\r\nyes\r\n\r\n5. Does the license steward support this submission, or is at least aware of and not in opposition of it?\r\nnot sure, probably doesn't matter for something this old\r\n\r\nSummary of factors / outcome\r\nI'm a bit torn here, as to the prevalence of use and how it is used in terms of the application of items on the SPDX License List.\r\n@samth - can you provide a bit more color as to how having an SPDX identifier for this would be helpful for context\r\n\r\nwill discuss further with SPDX legal","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/965954420/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/965973061","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1340#issuecomment-965973061","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1340","id":965973061,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE845k5RF","user":{"login":"samth","id":244723,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0NDcyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244723?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth","html_url":"https://github.com/samth","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samth/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-11-11T04:15:23Z","updated_at":"2021-11-11T04:15:23Z","body":"We came upon this issue while adding SPDX identifiers for the licenses of Racket packages, some of which include the text of, or text from, the Scheme reports. Adding it would make it possible to make these machine-processable. \r\n\r\nAn alternative that would work equally well would be to broaden the HaskellReport license identifier to include this one as well. That one is almost certainly derived from the text in the Scheme report and serves identical purposes. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/965973061/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/966549080","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1340#issuecomment-966549080","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1340","id":966549080,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE845nF5Y","user":{"login":"LiberalArtist","id":10700996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzAwOTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10700996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist","html_url":"https://github.com/LiberalArtist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-11-11T19:00:37Z","updated_at":"2021-11-11T19:00:37Z","body":"Re <https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1340#issuecomment-965954420>:\r\n>  -  If a software license, does it apply to source code and not only to executables?\r\n>      -  it refers to a report (not software)\r\n\r\nIt may be relevant that the Scheme reports, which serve as the standards for the Scheme programming language, include source code, not just prose. For example, [Appendix B: Sample definitions for derived forms](http://www.r6rs.org/final/html/r6rs/r6rs-Z-H-16.html#node_chap_B) of R6RS (2007) includes the following reference implementation for Scheme's `case` form, which could be used—directly or with modifications—by Scheme implementations that don't handle `case` as a compiler built-in:\r\n```scheme\r\n(define-syntax case\r\n  (syntax-rules (else)\r\n    ((case expr0\r\n       ((key ...) res1 res2 ...)\r\n       ...\r\n       (else else-res1 else-res2 ...))\r\n     (let ((tmp expr0))\r\n       (cond\r\n         ((memv tmp '(key ...)) res1 res2 ...)\r\n         ...\r\n         (else else-res1 else-res2 ...))))\r\n    ((case expr0\r\n       ((keya ...) res1a res2a ...)\r\n       ((keyb ...) res1b res2b ...)\r\n       ...)\r\n     (let ((tmp expr0))\r\n       (cond\r\n         ((memv tmp '(keya ...)) res1a res2a ...)\r\n         ((memv tmp '(keyb ...)) res1b res2b ...)\r\n         ...)))))\r\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/966549080/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/966575375","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1340#issuecomment-966575375","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/1340","id":966575375,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE845nMUP","user":{"login":"LiberalArtist","id":10700996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzAwOTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10700996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist","html_url":"https://github.com/LiberalArtist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LiberalArtist/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-11-11T19:43:08Z","updated_at":"2021-11-11T19:43:08Z","body":"Another example of the license in use is [`Scheme->C`](https://www.cs.cmu.edu/afs/cs/project/ai-repository/ai/lang/scheme/impl/scheme2c/0.html), a Scheme to C compiler by Joel Bartlett for DEC and HP. From the copyright file for the [Debian \"sid\" package `scheme2c-doc`](https://salsa.debian.org/debian/scheme2c/-/blob/1a34dc8a1c21418f82461594abc20cc9f869e72b/debian/copyright#L60-84):\r\n```\r\nThe documentation includes a copy of the R4RS manual, which states:\r\n\r\n  We intend this report to belong to the entire Scheme community, and\r\n  so we grant permission to copy it in whole or in part without fee.\r\n  In particular, we encourage implementors of Scheme to use this\r\n  report as a starting point for manuals and other documentation,\r\n  modifying it as necessary.\r\n\r\n  It was written and edited by:\r\n\r\n    William Clinger and Jonathan Rees (Editors)\r\n\r\n    H. Abelson       R. K. Dybvig     C. T. Haynes    G. J. Rozas\r\n    N. I. Adams IV   D. P. Friedman   E. Kohlbecker   G. L. Steele Jr.\r\n    D. H. Bartley    R. Halstead      D. Oxley        G. J. Sussman\r\n    G. Brooks        C. Hanson        K. M. Pitman    M. Wand\r\n\r\nThe R4RS sources include a LaTeX style file, algol60.sty, which states\r\n\r\n  % Copyright (C) 1985 by Leslie Lamport\r\n  % Hacked To Death (H) 1986 by Jonathan Rees from Lamport's REPORT and\r\n  %   REP11 document styles\r\n\r\nThis style file appears to be covered by the same permissive grant\r\nthat covers the remainder of the R4RS manual LaTeX source.\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/966575375/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":